ntities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n----Reports-----\ncommunity,full_content\r\n728,\"# Malnutrition Screening and Clinical Nutrition Community\n\nThis community is centered around the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) and its application in clinical nutrition, particularly for vulnerable populations such as the elderly and patients undergoing medical procedures. Key entities include healthcare professionals, organizations like ESPEN and BAPEN, and various nutritional assessment tools that are interconnected through their roles in identifying and managing malnutrition.\n\n## Centrality of the Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST)\n\nThe Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) is a pivotal entity in this community, widely utilized for assessing malnutrition risk across various healthcare settings. Developed by the British Association for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (BAPEN), MUST is recognized for its effectiveness in predicting clinical outcomes, including mortality and length of hospital stay, particularly among elderly patients. Its application spans hospitals, primary care, and specialized nutrition services, making it an essential resource for healthcare professionals aiming to address malnutrition. The tool's endorsement by organizations like ESPEN and ASPEN further underscores its significance in clinical practice [Data: Entities (559, 8017); Relationships (990, 2927, 3900, 3907, 3888, +more)].\n\n## Role of healthcare professionals in malnutrition management\n\nHealthcare professionals, referred to as 'personal sanitario', play a crucial role in the assessment and management of patients' nutritional status. This group includes doctors and nutritionists who utilize tools like MUST to evaluate malnutrition risk, particularly in vulnerable populations such as those undergoing hematopoietic cell transplants. Their involvement is essential for ensuring that patients receive appropriate nutritional interventions, which can significantly impact recovery and overall health outcomes. The integration of these professionals within the Sistema Nacional de Salud highlights the importance of coordinated care in addressing malnutrition [Data: Entities (13775); Relationships (1902, 3911, 3975, +more)].\n\n## Influence of organizations like ESPEN and BAPEN\n\nOrganizations such as the European Society of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ESPEN) and the British Association of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (BAPEN) are instrumental in advancing nutritional standards and practices. ESPEN's guidelines on clinical nutrition and BAPEN's development of the MUST tool reflect their commitment to improving nutritional care across Europe. These organizations provide essential resources and recommendations that inform healthcare professionals on best practices, thereby enhancing the quality of care for patients requiring nutritional support [Data: Entities (1634, 8017); Relationships (2927, 3904, 3907, +more)].\n\n## Diverse nutritional assessment tools in use\n\nThe community encompasses various nutritional assessment tools beyond MUST, such as the Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS2002) and the Rapid Screen. These tools are designed to identify nutritional risk in different populations, including the elderly and oncology patients. The use of multiple screening methods allows for a comprehensive approach to assessing nutritional status, ensuring that healthcare providers can tailor interventions to meet the specific needs of their patients. The interplay between these tools enhances the overall effectiveness of nutritional care [Data: Entities (721, 3286, 3283); Relationships (3898, 3903, 3886, +more)].\n\n## Impact of clinical guidelines on nutritional practices\n\nClinical guidelines developed by experts like Forbes A and Compher C significantly influence nutritional practices in healthcare settings. Their contributions to the international consensus on malnutrition and various clinical guidelines ensure that healthcare professionals are equipped with the latest evidence-based practices for managing malnutrition. This ongoing discourse among experts is vital for adapting nutritional strategies to meet the evolving needs of patients, particularly those with complex medical conditions [Data: Entities (719, 717); Relationships (2928, 5011, 3894, +more)].\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n560,MINI NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT,\"The Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA) is a structured and practical questionnaire designed for the early detection of malnutrition or risk of malnutrition in elderly individuals, both in outpatient settings and institutionalized environments. This tool is particularly valuable in geriatric evaluations, as it includes a dietary questionnaire and is recognized for its high sensitivity in assessing nutritional status. The MNA is validated specifically for elderly populations and is recommended by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) for use in both institutionalized and non-institutionalized individuals.\n\nThe MNA serves to classify patients based on their nutritional risk, helping healthcare providers identify those at risk of malnutrition. It evaluates various aspects of nutritional status and is linked to criteria of frailty, making it an essential component of comprehensive geriatric assessments. Overall, the Mini Nutritional Assessment is a non-invasive tool that plays a crucial role in identifying and addressing malnutrition in the elderly.\",24\r\n551,CRIBADO NUTRICIONAL,\"CRIBADO NUTRICIONAL refers to the nutritional screening process, which is essential for identifying patients at risk of malnutrition. This process is particularly relevant for individuals with oropharyngeal dysphagia and those undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation. Nutritional screening is a standardized procedure that evaluates the nutritional status of patients, making it a mandatory practice in hospital settings. The primary goal of this screening is to identify individuals who may benefit from nutritional support, ensuring that at-risk patients receive the necessary care to prevent malnutrition.\",6\r\n270,PREDYCES STUDY,\"The PREDyCES Study is a comprehensive research initiative that investigates the prevalence and costs associated with malnutrition in hospitalized patients, specifically focusing on those with diabetes mellitus and dysphagia. This study aims to analyze the extent of hospital malnutrition among these patient groups, highlighting the significant health and economic implications of this condition in a hospital setting. Through its multifaceted approach, the PREDyCES Study seeks to provide valuable insights into the challenges posed by malnutrition in healthcare, ultimately contributing to improved patient care and resource allocation.\",7\r\n3228,ANCIANOS,\"Ancianos refers to elderly individuals, particularly those who are at risk of malnutrition, especially the frail. This group has specific dietary recommendations aimed at managing diabetes, highlighting the importance of tailored nutrition to support their health and well-being.\",6\r\n7699,BRITISH JOURNAL OF NUTRITION,\"The British Journal of Nutrition is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on nutrition and its significant impact on health. It covers a wide range of topics, including the effects of dietary fats on health, the relationship between nutrition and various health conditions, and the implications of nutritional status for health outcomes. The journal features studies on specific populations, such as stroke patients and individuals with liver cirrhosis, as well as broader research on energy expenditure and other nutritional factors. Overall, the British Journal of Nutrition serves as a vital resource for advancing knowledge in the field of nutrition and its effects on health.\",10\r\n561,MALNUTRITION SCREENING TOOL,\"The Malnutrition Screening Tool (MST) is an Australian-origin method specifically designed to assess the risk of malnutrition in patients, particularly those with swallowing difficulties and oncology patients. It is validated for use in clinical settings and focuses on recent appetite changes and weight loss to identify malnutrition risk. The MST serves as a comprehensive screening tool that aids healthcare professionals in recognizing malnutrition in patients, ensuring timely intervention and management.\",11\r\n8016,MALNUTRITION SYNDROMES,\"Malnutrition syndromes refer to a range of conditions that arise from inadequate nutrition, impacting clinical outcomes and healthcare costs.\",5\r\n568,NESTLÉ NUTRITION INSTITUTE,\"The Nestlé Nutrition Institute is an organization dedicated to nutritional research, assessment, and education. It focuses on evaluating and treating nutritional status, offering tools such as the Mini Nutritional Assessment to help healthcare professionals assess patients' nutritional needs. The institute aims to enhance understanding and awareness of nutrition, particularly in the context of malnutrition, by providing resources and support for effective nutritional screening and intervention.\",3\r\n3242,GERIATRIC NUTRITIONAL RISK INDEX,\"The Geriatric Nutritional Risk Index (GNRI) is a specialized index utilized to assess the nutritional status of elderly patients and to predict various clinical outcomes. It is particularly designed to evaluate the prognosis of hospitalized elderly individuals, focusing on their nutritional needs. The GNRI serves as a critical tool in predicting morbidity and mortality among elderly patients who are receiving nutritional support, thereby aiding healthcare providers in making informed decisions regarding patient care and intervention strategies.\",4\r\n578,CONSENSO MULTIDISCIPLINAR,The Consenso Multidisciplinar sobre el Abordaje de la Desnutrición Hospitalaria en España is a guideline aimed at addressing hospital malnutrition through a multidisciplinary approach.,2\r\n16613,EQUIPO DE SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL,The Nutritional Support Team (ESN) is responsible for providing nutritional support and care in a clinical setting.,4\r\n715,JENSEN GL,\"Jensen GL is a prominent researcher and author in the field of nutritional assessment and malnutrition. He has made significant contributions to the understanding of malnutrition syndromes and their implications in clinical practice. Additionally, Jensen GL has been actively involved in the development of clinical practice guidelines for diagnosing malnutrition, further establishing his expertise and influence in this critical area of healthcare.\",5\r\n16584,RUBENSTEIN LZ,\"Rubenstein LZ is a researcher and author who is actively involved in the development of screening tools for undernutrition in geriatric practice. Their work focuses on addressing the critical issue of undernutrition among the elderly, contributing valuable insights and methodologies to improve the assessment and management of this condition in healthcare settings.\",2\r\n714,SOCIETY ESPAÑOLA DE NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL Y ENTERAL,The Sociedad Española de Nutrición Parenteral y Enteral (SENPE) promotes multidisciplinary consensus on the approach to hospital malnutrition in Spain.,4\r\n3250,NUTRITION SCREENING INITIATIVE,The Nutrition Screening Initiative is a program designed to enhance the nutritional health of older adults by implementing screening and intervention strategies.,3\r\n8024,COMMUNITY,\"The community refers to a group of individuals living in a common area, where nutritional assessments can also be applied.\",1\r\n1702,CRIBADO DEFINITIVO,The Cribado Definitivo is a screening process that assesses nutritional status and severity of illness based on specific criteria and scoring.,1\r\n567,EVALUACIÓN GERIÁTRICA INTEGRAL,A comprehensive assessment approach for elderly patients that includes nutritional evaluation as a key component.,1\r\n722,TOULOUSE FRAILTY PLATFORM,The Toulouse Frailty Platform is a research initiative focused on frailty and nutritional assessment in elderly populations.,1\r\n8023,MINI NUTRITIONAL ASSESSMENT SHORT FORM,\"Mini Nutritional Assessment Short Form is a validated independent screening tool based on the long version of the MNA, designed to reduce assessment time and can be used regularly in various patient settings.\",1\r\n1840,VELLAS B,\"Vellas B is a prominent researcher specializing in the fields of frailty and aging. He has made significant contributions to the development and review of the Mini Nutritional Assessment, which is widely used in clinical settings to evaluate nutritional status. Additionally, Vellas B is an author of the ESPEN guidelines for nutrition screening, further underscoring his expertise and influence in the area of nutritional assessment and its applications in healthcare.\",1\r\n565,CUIDADO CLÍNICOS RUTINARIOS,Routine clinical care practices that include monitoring and managing patients' nutritional needs.,1\r\n7716,CHAJES V,An author who has studied the association between fatty acids and breast cancer risk.,1\r\n3229,CRIBADO DE DESNUTRICIÓN,\"\"\"CRIBADO DE DESNUTRICIÓN\"\" refers to a screening process designed to identify individuals at risk of malnutrition. This nutritional screening is particularly important in clinical settings, where it is recommended to be conducted in hospitals, especially for elderly patients. The primary goal of this process is to detect malnutrition early, allowing for timely intervention and support to improve the nutritional status of at-risk individuals.\",4\r\n713,ALIANZA MÁS NUTRIDOS,\"Alianza más nutridos is an organization focused on nutritional efficacy and combating malnutrition in various settings, including hospitals and communities.\",2\r\n6452,STUDY VIDA,Study VIDA group focuses on the application of the new ESPEN definition of malnutrition in geriatric diabetic patients during hospitalization.,1\r\n3231,PROCESO DE VALORACIÓN NUTRICIONAL,\"The assessment process to evaluate nutritional status, which is crucial for elderly patients\",1\r\n16614,U.G.C DE ENDOCRINOLOGÍA Y NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA,The Clinical Endocrinology and Nutrition Unit (U.G.C) specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of nutritional disorders.,2\r\n8013,BISTR